# LED triggers for the Avast Omni RECOVERY slot (p7).
#
# Deliberately DIFFERENT from the A/B slots' rules, so the LED pattern answers
# "which slot am I on?" without a login. On a headless appliance that is the
# only signal available before you have a shell, and knowing you are in
# recovery changes what you should do next.
#
#   A/B slots:  power breathing, app1 flickering with network traffic, app2 dark
#   recovery:   power breathing, app1 AND app2 SOLID
#
# Two steady lights that are never both on in normal operation. You can see it
# across a room, through a cupboard door, without a serial cable.
#
#   power -> heartbeat     Still means "alive", same as the A/B slots. Recovery
#                          having a different liveness signal would be actively
#                          confusing.
#   app1  -> default-on    Solid. Together with app2 this is the recovery tell.
#   app2  -> default-on    Not "panic" as in the A/B rules: in recovery the
#                          steady pair is worth more than a panic indicator, and
#                          if this slot panics you are already at the bottom of
#                          the recovery ladder with a serial cable in hand.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="leds", KERNEL=="apollo:power", ATTR{trigger}="heartbeat"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="leds", KERNEL=="apollo:app1",  ATTR{trigger}="default-on"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="leds", KERNEL=="apollo:app2",  ATTR{trigger}="default-on"
